+// thread of its own, which sends them in order: the loop's core does not
+// pay for the send's work in the kernel, which is most of a server's. The
+// loop puts posts on a ring and the writer takes them off, each side moving
+// its own index; a writer with nothing to do spins a while, then sleeps on
+// its bell, with its sleep flag up for the loop to ring it. A post of NULL
+// closes the fd, after what was posted before.
